To install Argo CD on Ubuntu with Minikube/Kubernetes:

1. Create the Argo CD namespace
Shell
kubectl create namespace argocd
2. Install Argo CD
Shell
kubectl apply -n argocd -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml
3. Verify pods
Shell
kubectl get pods -n argocd

Wait until all pods show:

Plain Text
Running

Example:

Plain Text
argocd-server
argocd-repo-server
argocd-application-controller
argocd-redis
4. Check services
Shell
kubectl get svc -n argocd
5. Access Argo CD UI

For your Codespace VM:

Shell
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443 --address 0.0.0.0

Then:

Open PORTS tab in Codespaces.
Find port 8080.
Set visibility to Public.
Open the forwarded URL.
6. Get admin password
Shell
kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret \
-o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d && echo
7. Login
Plain Text
Username: admin
Password: <password from command above>
Install Argo CD CLI

Download:

Shell
curl -sSL -o argocd \
https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-linux-amd64

Make executable:

Shell
chmod +x argocd

Move to PATH:

Shell
sudo mv argocd /usr/local/bin/

Verify:

Shell
argocd version
Login from CLI
Shell
argocd login localhost:8080 --username admin --insecure
 
Verify installation
Shell
kubectl get all -n argocd
 
Shell
kubectl get pods -n argocd
Shell
kubectl get svc -n argocd

If you're using GitHub Codespaces, access issues are usually related to port forwarding. The Argo CD installation itself is complete once all argocd-* pods are in the Running state.
